    "long_instructions": "## Filter Data\r\n\r\nA condition checks each value in a column and returns a **Boolean value**: `True` or `False`. A filter keeps only the rows where the condition is `True`.\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 1]\r\nRun the program. Compare the Boolean values in the first output with the rows in the filtered DataFrame. What connection do you notice?\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 2]\r\nModify the condition to find superheroes whose `Alias` ends with `\"n\"` instead of `\"r\"`. Run the program and observe how both outputs change.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 3]\r\nModify the code to check which superheroes have a `City` that ends with `\"City\"`. Print the Boolean condition and the filtered DataFrame.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 4]\r\nHow do the `True` and `False` values determine which rows appear in the filtered DataFrame?\r\n:::",
    "ai_tutor_available": "false",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
